{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 114, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is already absent, removing edge 4 cuts the last intermediate path into the output node and collapses accuracy (exp 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, deleting edge 5 leaves node 3 fed only by edge 3, which wrecks the network (exp 94)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pool on the direct input-output edge with a 3x3 conv adds far more capacity than replacing another op (exp 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a pooling edge into the output for a 3x3 conv gives large gains (exps 35, 70), much more than swapping from other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Converting the node1->node2 pool into a conv adds learnable depth (exp 96), whereas replacing a 1x1 conv gives little or negative change (exp 27)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with pooling removes key capacity (exps 18, 54), while replacing skip or 1x1 costs less."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Losing a 3x3 conv on edge 1 to pooling is much more harmful (exp 42) than adding pooling where there was none or a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on a missing edge 0 activates node 1's downstream paths with learned features, giving big gains (exp 43)."}, {"edit_e